WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.462
Third-party dependencies are part of the application risk surface.

2
00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:09.928
Teams need visibility into which packages, frameworks, images, and services are used and where they are deployed.

3
00:00:09.928 --> 00:00:15.496
Unsupported software becomes difficult to defend because fixes may no longer be available.

4
00:00:15.496 --> 00:00:23.129
End-of-life frameworks, runtimes, plugins, and operating systems should be replaced or isolated according to risk.

5
00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:30.692
Supply chain risk includes vulnerable packages, malicious updates, compromised build tools, and untrusted images.

6
00:00:30.692 --> 00:00:35.910
SaaS teams should govern package sources and build processes as part of system operations.

7
00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.749
Dependency tracking supports timely response when new vulnerabilities are announced.

8
00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:47.724
Remediation decisions should consider exploitability, exposure, compensating controls, and customer impact.

9
00:00:47.724 --> 00:00:50.558
Maintain software inventory and ownership.

10
00:00:50.558 --> 00:00:53.182
Use patch management and dependency scanning.

11
00:00:53.182 --> 00:00:56.604
Prioritize remediation based on risk and exposure.

12
00:00:56.604 --> 00:01:00.715
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC7.

13
00:01:00.715 --> 00:01:03.519
1 - Vulnerability management; CC8.

14
00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:04.896
1 - Change management.
